d 'CAUSALREP': module for quantifying the internal validity and representativeness of OLS, IV, and two-way fixed-effects estimands
d
d  causalrep implements diagnostics for quantifying the internal
d validity and representativeness of weighted estimands developed
d by Poirier and Słoczyński (2026). It computes the measure of
d internal validity (MIV), defined as the largest possible share of
d the relevant target population for which an ordinary
d least-squares (OLS), instrumental-variables (IV), or two-way
d fixed-effects (TWFE) estimand can be represented as an average
d treatment effect. Where applicable, it also computes the measure
d of representativeness (MR), defined as the corresponding largest
d possible share of the entire population. The target population is
d the entire population for OLS, the complier population for IV,
d and the treated population for TWFE. The package can also compute
d these measures conditional on user-supplied conditional average
d treatment effects. 
d
d KW: weighted estimands
d KW: internal validity
d KW: representativeness
d KW: heterogeneous treatment effects
d KW: ordinary least squares
d KW: instrumental variables
d KW: two-way fixed effects
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260726
d
d Author:  Tymon Słoczyński , Brandeis University
d Support: email tslocz@@brandeis.edu
d
f causalrep.ado
f causalrep.sthlp
f causalrep_did.sthlp
f causalrep_iv.sthlp
f causalrep_ols.sthlp
f ../_/_causalrep_ols.ado
f ../_/_causalrep_did.ado
f ../_/_causalrep_iv.ado
